Advanced dynamic model reduction and validation (@pe-dynamic-model-study: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electrical-power-engineering, #source "../sources/Power-System-Dynamics-and-Control-Kulkarni.lingua#r_2T4WS3TCPCXRB5JEH7HTN5FAHQ", #source "../sources/Hybrid-Symbolic-Numeric-Power-Models-Cui.lingua#r_7XTYA62FQ8W2X448XXVFNPA7AK", #source "../sources/ANDES-Modeling-and-Analysis-Manual.lingua#r_5JM9DVGXWSD8645484SZP5XRSZ", #source "../sources/DPsim-Transient-and-Dynamic-Phasor-Methods.lingua#r_6Y8PGZBGJHGV3JHZ1Q8XC77RR3", #electrical-power-engineering "../study/An-integrated-electrical-power-system-investigation.lingua#r_06BN864FF9C0AN3EWZJE78Y6Y3") { r_5FJVP1QJJGERMWXP37CKC4BZZJ
**Read:** [Power System Dynamics and Control — A. M. Kulkarni](../sources/Power-System-Dynamics-and-Control-Kulkarni.lingua#r_2T4WS3TCPCXRB5JEH7HTN5FAHQ), entire programme; [Hybrid Symbolic-Numeric Framework — Cui, Li and Tomsovic](../sources/Hybrid-Symbolic-Numeric-Power-Models-Cui.lingua#r_7XTYA62FQ8W2X448XXVFNPA7AK), entire paper and complete applicable validation case; [ANDES — dynamic modelling and analysis manual](../sources/ANDES-Modeling-and-Analysis-Manual.lingua#r_5JM9DVGXWSD8645484SZP5XRSZ), whole relevant model/initialization/analysis methods; [DPsim — electromagnetic-transient and dynamic-phasor methods](../sources/DPsim-Transient-and-Dynamic-Phasor-Methods.lingua#r_6Y8PGZBGJHGV3JHZ1Q8XC77RR3), whole applicable domain/model and solver documentation.

Complete all of [Power System Dynamics and Control — A. M. Kulkarni](../sources/Power-System-Dynamics-and-Control-Kulkarni.lingua#r_2T4WS3TCPCXRB5JEH7HTN5FAHQ) and the full applicable [ANDES — dynamic modelling and analysis manual](../sources/ANDES-Modeling-and-Analysis-Manual.lingua#r_5JM9DVGXWSD8645484SZP5XRSZ), [Hybrid Symbolic-Numeric Framework — Cui, Li and Tomsovic](../sources/Hybrid-Symbolic-Numeric-Power-Models-Cui.lingua#r_7XTYA62FQ8W2X448XXVFNPA7AK) and [DPsim — electromagnetic-transient and dynamic-phasor methods](../sources/DPsim-Transient-and-Dynamic-Phasor-Methods.lingua#r_6Y8PGZBGJHGV3JHZ1Q8XC77RR3) methods. Choose a bounded source/control/network problem whose observables span more than one time scale. Derive a classical/RMS model, an appropriate more detailed model and their consistent operating initialization.

Compare state meaning, bases, energy, algebraic constraints, events/limits and numerical error. Use independent Jacobians, an analytical mode or energy limit, time-step refinement and a differently formulated calculation. The original fault-clearing model supplies a fully inspectable restricted benchmark, not a validation of every new controller or event.

Demonstrate where a reduction succeeds and where it misses a measured/published or independently modelled effect, such as an excitation limit, converter current transition or fast network transient. Predict a changed parameter/operating state not used in calibration and quantify uncertainty. Explain whether a discrepancy is numerical, parametric or structural. The final scholarly account should show exactly which practical stability or response claim each model can support, instead of ranking models solely by complexity or a solver's reputation.

**Continue:** [An integrated electrical-power-system investigation](../study/An-integrated-electrical-power-system-investigation.lingua#r_06BN864FF9C0AN3EWZJE78Y6Y3).

**Return:** [Electrical power engineering — sources, networks, machines and continuing service](../Electrical-power-engineering.lingua#r_300EPNGATK7PHWNZCQFBXGZFCQ).
